{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>ולרבקה</b> Two times in the Masorah: one at the beginning of a verse — ולרבקה; and one at the end of a verse — ותהיין מורת רוח ליצחק ולרבקה. For his eyes were dim from the smoke of Esau's idolatry, but to Rebekah it did not cause harm, for she had seen the like in her father's house, for he was a priest to idolatry. Therefore Scripture placed Isaac's name first, to teach that they were not a grief of spirit to Rebekah as to Isaac. Or another interpretation: a hint to what they said — one who takes a wife should investigate her brothers, for most children resemble the mother's brothers. And because her brother was wicked, she bore Esau the wicked. And this is: ולרבקה אח ושמו לבן / ותהיין מורת רוח ליצחק ולרבקה."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:49.241188175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}